/-!
# Tag 0A0L in one statement: both equalities, at `H^p(U, K^∧)`

Let `X` be a locally Noetherian scheme, `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪_X` a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals and `K` a
pseudo-coherent object of `D(𝒪_X)` with derived completion `K^∧`. [Stacks, Tag 0A0L] asserts

`H^p(U, K^∧) = lim H^p(U, K)/IⁿH^p(U, K) = H^p(U, K)^∧`

for every affine open `U ⊂ X`, where `I = ℐ(U)` and the completion on the right is the derived
completion of the `Γ(X, U)`-module `H^p(U, K)` along `I`. This file proves both equalities in one
statement and carries the tag.

## What was missing, and what closes it

`Completion/FormalFunctionsPseudoCoherent.lean` proves the second equality outright, and
`Completion/FormalFunctionsPseudoCoherentModuleSide.lean` the first one with its left hand side
read at the derived completion in `D(Γ(X, U))` of `RΓ(U, K)` rather than at `RΓ(U, K^∧)`; its
`exists_adjunction_and_homology_derivedSections_derivedCompletion_iso_adicCompletion`
is the transport of the first onto `H^p(U, K^∧)` **given** the identification

`RΓ(U, K^∧) = RΓ(U, K)^∧`,

which is [Stacks, Tag 0CQI]. Three results close that gap, each proved separately:

* [Stacks, Tag 0CQI] itself, at a sheaf of ideals of finite type,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.nonempty_iso_derivedSectionsOverObject_derivedCompletion`;
* `Stacks.Algebraization.isFiniteType_idealSheafSiteSubmodule` — a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals
  of a locally Noetherian scheme is of finite type, so [Stacks, Tag 099F] produces `K^∧` along the
  tag's own `ℐ` — together with
  `Stacks.Algebraization.exists_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal_affine`, which supplies that
  tag's generation hypothesis at an affine open, with the generated ideal equal to `ℐ(U)` on the
  nose;
* `Stacks.Algebraization.derivedSectionsOverSiteIso` — the two models of `RΓ(U, -)` the two tags
  are stated in agree.

So the ideal along which the module side is completed is the tag's own `I = ℐ(U)`, not merely the
ideal generated by a chosen family: a Noetherian `Γ(X, U)` lets the family be chosen to generate
`ℐ(U)`, and `exists_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal_affine` chooses it so. The source's warning
that the two ideals may differ is about a general object of a general site; over an affine open of
a locally Noetherian scheme they can be made to agree.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Algebraization.nonempty_iso_derivedSections_derivedCompletion_affine`: the
  identification `RΓ(U, K^∧) ≅ RΓ(U, K)^∧` of [Stacks, Tag 0CQI] at an affine open of a locally
  Noetherian scheme, read in the schemes-level model of `RΓ(U, -)` and for every reflector onto
  the derived-complete objects of `D(Γ(X, U))`.
* `Stacks.Algebraization.exists_iso_homology_derivedSections_derivedCompletion_whole`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 0A0L]** — both equalities.

## Implementation notes

`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfSection` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfTerminalSection` are the two spellings of "a section
over `U`, read as a global section of the structure sheaf of the slice `𝒞/U`"; the generation
hypothesis is produced in the first and consumed in the second, and
`Stacks.Algebraization.globalSectionOfSection_eq_globalSectionOfTerminalSection` identifies them.

Derived completion of `Γ(X, U)`-modules is produced, not assumed: `Γ(X, U)` is Noetherian, so
[Stacks, Tag 0920] applies, and the statement's first conjunct exhibits a reflector while the
second holds for every one of them.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0L](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0L)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CQI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CQI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A06](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A06)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0920](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0920)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.SheafOfModules (opensRingedSite)
open Stacks.Cohomology.HypercohomologyEdge (derivedSections)
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

universe u

namespace Stacks.Algebraization

attribute [local instance 100000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-- **The two spellings of "a section over `U`, read as a global section of `𝒪_U`" agree.** One
restricts the section along the structure arrow of an object of `𝒞/U`, the other along the unique
arrow to the terminal object `𝟙_U`; those are the same arrow. -/
theorem globalSectionOfSection_eq_globalSectionOfTerminalSection
    (Y : AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.{u, u, u}) (V : Y.C) (a : Y.O.obj.obj (op V)) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfSection Y V a =
      AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfTerminalSection
        (X := Y.over V) Over.mkIdTerminal a := by
  refine (Presheaf.globalSectionsEquivSections _).injective (Subtype.ext (funext fun W => ?_))
  refine (AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfSection Y V a W).trans ?_
  refine Eq.trans ?_
    (AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfTerminalSection
      (X := Y.over V) Over.mkIdTerminal a W).symm
  have hleft : (Over.mkIdTerminal.from (unop W)).left = (unop W).hom := by
    simp
  change (CommRingCat.Hom.hom (Y.O.obj.map ((unop W).hom).op)) a =
    (CommRingCat.Hom.hom (Y.O.obj.map ((Over.mkIdTerminal.from (unop W)).left).op)) a
  rw [hleft]

-- The instance putting [Stacks, Tag 099F]'s derived completion at the small Zariski site of a
-- locally Noetherian scheme, along a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals, is
-- `Stacks.Algebraization.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_idealSheafSiteSubmodule` of
-- `Completion/CoherentCompletionAffineSections.lean`, imported above, and it is deliberately not
-- redeclared here under the same fully-qualified name. Two declarations sharing a
-- fully-qualified name across modules do not break the build, but they do change which one
-- instance search finds, and that then depends on import order. Such duplicates are found
-- only by listing the fully-qualified names declared in two or more modules;
-- a check that compares declaration bodies rather than names
-- cannot detect them.

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (𝓘 : X.IdealSheafData)
  (K : DerivedCategory X.Modules) (U : X.affineOpens)

/-- **[Stacks, Tag 0CQI] at an affine open of a locally Noetherian scheme**, in the schemes-level
model of `RΓ(U, -)` and for every reflector onto the derived-complete objects of `D(Γ(X, U))`:

`RΓ(U, K^∧) ≅ RΓ(U, K)^∧`,

the completion on the left along `ℐ` and the one on the right along `I = ℐ(U)`.

Three steps. A Noetherian `Γ(X, U)` provides a finite family generating `ℐ(U)` whose associated
global sections of `𝒪_U` generate `ℐ|_U`
(`Stacks.Algebraization.exists_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal_affine`), which is the
generation hypothesis of [Stacks, Tag 0CQI]; that tag then gives the identification in the
ringed-site model of `RΓ(U, -)` and with the completion
`DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletionFunctor` along that family; and
`Stacks.Algebraization.derivedSectionsOverSiteIso` carries it to the schemes-level model while
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.isoOfReflection` replaces the named completion by an arbitrary
reflector, both being reflections of `D(Γ(X, U))` onto the objects derived complete along
`ℐ(U)`. -/
theorem nonempty_iso_derivedSections_derivedCompletion_affine :
    let P : ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, U.1))) :=
      fun L ↦ IsDerivedComplete (𝓘.ideal U) L
    ∀ (C : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, U.1)) ⥤ P.FullSubcategory) (_ : C ⊣ P.ι),
      Nonempty
        ((derivedSections (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace) U.1).obj
            ((AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletion (opensRingedSite X.sheaf)
              (idealSheafSiteSubmodule 𝓘)).obj K) ≅
          (C ⋙ P.ι).obj
            ((derivedSections (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace) U.1).obj K)) := by
  have : IsNoetherianRing Γ(X, U.1) := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian U
  have : HasProductsOfShape ℕ (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, U.1))) :=
    Stacks.DerivedProducts.hasProductsOfShape_derivedCategory
  obtain ⟨n, g, hg, hspan, hgen⟩ := exists_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal_affine 𝓘 U
  rw [← hspan]
  intro P C adj
  -- [Stacks, Tag 0CQI] in the ringed-site model of `RΓ(U, -)`.
  obtain ⟨e₀⟩ :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.nonempty_iso_derivedSectionsOverObject_derivedCompletion
      (opensRingedSite X.sheaf) (idealSheafSiteSubmodule 𝓘) U.1 g
      (fun i => (mem_idealSheafSiteSubmodule_obj_affine 𝓘 U (g i)).2 (hg i))
      (by
        refine Eq.trans ?_ hgen.symm
        exact congrArg (AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealOfGlobalSections _)
          (funext fun i => (globalSectionOfSection_eq_globalSectionOfTerminalSection
            (opensRingedSite X.sheaf) U.1 (g i)).symm))
      K
  -- The two models of `RΓ(U, -)` agree.
  have Φ := derivedSectionsOverSiteIso (X := X) U.1
  -- The named completion along `g` is a reflection onto the objects derived complete along
  -- `ℐ(U) = (g_1, …, g_n)`, so it is identified with the arbitrary reflector `C`.
  refine ⟨(Φ.app _).symm ≪≫ e₀ ≪≫
    (ObjectProperty.isoOfReflection
      (fun L ↦ IsDerivedComplete (Ideal.span (Set.range g)) L)
      adj.unit (DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletionUnit Γ(X, U.1) g)
      (fun Z ↦ (C.obj Z).property)
      (DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletion_isReflection Γ(X, U.1) g).1
      (fun Z E' hE' ↦ ObjectProperty.bijective_precomp_adjunction_unit _ adj Z E' hE')
      (DerivedCompletion.derivedCompletion_isReflection Γ(X, U.1) g).2 _).symm ≪≫
    (C ⋙ P.ι).mapIso (Φ.app K)⟩

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0A0L.** Let `X` be a locally Noetherian scheme, `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪_X` a
quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals and `K` a pseudo-coherent object of `D(𝒪_X)` with derived
completion `K^∧`. Then for every affine open `U ⊂ X`, with `A = Γ(X, U)` and `I = ℐ(U)`, and
every `p`,

`H^p(U, K^∧) = lim H^p(U, K)/IⁿH^p(U, K) = H^p(U, K)^∧`,

the completion on the right being the derived completion of the `A`-module `H^p(U, K)` along `I`,
read in degree zero.

Both equalities, at the source's own hypotheses. The first is
`exists_adjunction_and_homology_derivedSections_derivedCompletion_iso_adicCompletion`
with its input — the identification `RΓ(U, K^∧) = RΓ(U, K)^∧` of [Stacks, Tag 0CQI] — discharged by
`Stacks.Algebraization.nonempty_iso_derivedSections_derivedCompletion_affine`; the second is
`Stacks.Algebraization.adicCompletion_homology_derivedSections_iso_derivedCompletion`, which is
[Stacks, Tag 0A06] for the finite module `H^p(U, K)` placed in degree zero. Pseudo-coherence and
the locally Noetherian hypothesis enter through the finiteness of `H^n(U, K)`, which is
`Stacks.Algebraization.finite_homology_derivedSections_of_isPseudoCoherent`.

Derived completion of `A`-modules is produced, not assumed: the first conjunct exhibits a left
adjoint `C` to the inclusion of the derived-complete objects of `D(A)`, by
`Stacks.Algebraization.exists_derivedCompletionAdjunction`, and the second holds for every such
`C`, so no choice of reflector enters. The derived completion `K^∧` on `D(𝒪_X)` is produced too:
`ℐ` is of finite type on a locally Noetherian scheme
(`Stacks.Algebraization.isFiniteType_idealSheafSiteSubmodule`), so the reflector of [Stacks,
Tag 099F] exists along the tag's own ideal sheaf. -/
@[stacks 0A0L "the whole lemma, at the source's own hypotheses — `X` a locally Noetherian \
scheme, `𝓘 ⊂ 𝒪_X` a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals and `K` a pseudo-coherent object of \
`D(𝒪_X)`: for every affine open `U`, with `A = Γ(X, U)` and `I = 𝓘(U)`, and every `p`, both \
equalities `H^p(U, K^∧) = lim H^p(U, K)/IⁿH^p(U, K) = H^p(U, K)^∧`, the right hand completion \
being the derived completion of the A-module H^p(U,K) along I read in degree zero. The left hand \
side is read at the derived completion `K^∧` on `D(𝒪_X)` along `𝓘` itself, which exists because \
a quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals of a locally Noetherian scheme is of finite type, so [Stacks, \
Tag 099F] applies; the passage `RΓ(U, K^∧) = RΓ(U, K)^∧` is [Stacks, Tag 0CQI] at an affine \
open, where the chosen generating family spans `𝓘(U)` itself. The reflector onto the \
derived-complete objects of D(A) is produced out of [Stacks, Tag 0920] and the conclusion \
quantifies over it"]
theorem exists_iso_homology_derivedSections_derivedCompletion_whole
    (hK : RingedSpace.IsPseudoCoherent (X := X.toRingedSpace) K) (p : ℤ) :
    let P : ObjectProperty (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, U.1))) :=
      fun L ↦ IsDerivedComplete (𝓘.ideal U) L
    let Hp := fun (L : DerivedCategory X.Modules) ↦
      (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, U.1)) p).obj
        ((derivedSections (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace) U.1).obj L)
    (∃ C : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, U.1)) ⥤ P.FullSubcategory,
        Nonempty (C ⊣ P.ι)) ∧
      ∀ (C : DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, U.1)) ⥤ P.FullSubcategory) (_ : C ⊣ P.ι),
        Nonempty
          (Hp ((AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletion (opensRingedSite X.sheaf)
              (idealSheafSiteSubmodule 𝓘)).obj K) ≅
            ModuleCat.of Γ(X, U.1) (AdicCompletion (𝓘.ideal U) (Hp K))) ∧
        Nonempty
          (ModuleCat.of Γ(X, U.1) (AdicCompletion (𝓘.ideal U) (Hp K)) ≅
            (DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, U.1)) 0).obj
              ((C ⋙ P.ι).obj
                ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, U.1)) 0).obj (Hp K)))) := by
  intro P Hp
  have : IsNoetherianRing Γ(X, U.1) := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian U
  refine ⟨exists_derivedCompletionAdjunction Γ(X, U.1) (𝓘.ideal U), fun C adj => ⟨?_, ?_⟩⟩
  · obtain ⟨-, h⟩ :=
      exists_adjunction_and_homology_derivedSections_derivedCompletion_iso_adicCompletion X 𝓘 K
      ((AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletion (opensRingedSite X.sheaf)
        (idealSheafSiteSubmodule 𝓘)).obj K) hK U p
    exact h C adj (nonempty_iso_derivedSections_derivedCompletion_affine 𝓘 K U C adj)
  · obtain ⟨-, h⟩ :=
      exists_adjunction_and_adicCompletion_homology_derivedSections_iso_derivedCompletion
        X 𝓘 K hK U p
    exact h C adj

end Stacks.Algebraization

end
